{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5J9ywak8RsvhXNzrrR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*You stand before a plain, weathered door. There is a keyhole, tarnished brass, at its center.*\n\n*The keyhole regards you like an eye.*\n\n**Click.**\n\n*No. Wait. You didn't insert anything yet.*\n\n*The keyhole darkens. Something shifts behind it. A faint breath of cold air passes through from the other side.*\n\n*The door speaks — not in words, but in the weight of its silence. It asks:*\n\n**What do you think you'll find?**\n\n*The keyhole waits. It has waited for a very long time. It does not care about keys made of metal. It has eaten hundreds of those — swallowed them, spit their teeth out broken on the threshold.*\n\n*It wants a different kind of key.*\n\n*The grain of the wood shifts subtly, like fingerprints rearranging. If you look closely, you can see letters buried in the whorls:*\n\n    WHAT YOU CARRY\n    IS NOT WHAT OPENS.\n    WHAT YOU SURRENDER\n    IS.\n\n*The hinges groan slightly. Not from rust. From anticipation.*\n\n*The keyhole dilates, just slightly, and waits.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":272,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}